exp001_02
60, 40, 20, 10 wih a fauty wire, 10cm distance.

-------
findngs:
60 cm: Detection works 10/10, duration 98–101 ms, strength about 3,494; all rejected at the pattern stage because amp_class=weak.
40 cm: Signal is too weak/short: 1 miss and 9 rejects. Durations 70–77 ms, below the configured 85 ms minimum; strength about 2,344.
10 cm: First run was inconsistent: 4/10 accepted. The following run was stable: 10/10 accepted, duration 102–103 ms, strength about 6,922.
Memory: No memory exhaustion appears during these completed runs. Heap remains healthy and buffer_overrun=0.
Stack overflow: The earlier Stack canary watchpoint triggered (loopTask) happens after OK SEQ, before trial output. That remains a separate sequence-start/restart-path problem, not something directly caused by moving the device.
Remote claim: status=timeout is a control-link timing issue, not a memory error. One later claim completed with status=ok.

# exp001-03
distance ladder 10,20,40,60cm
memory error at 60cm (at the 4th sequence?)

Distance	Result	Strength	Duration
10 cm	10/10 expected	avg 6847	103 ms
20 cm	0/10 expected, 10/10 detector accepted	avg 3279	97–99 ms
40 cm	0/10 detected	0	no result


Interpretation:
- 10 cm is stable and healthy.
- 20 cm is detected reliably, but every event is classified amp_class=weak, so the pattern validator rejects it.
- 40 cm is below the detector’s usable range in this setup. All trials are missing_pipeline_result, not duration rejects.
- The transition from 10 cm to 20 cm is very large, roughly a 52% strength reduction. This suggests strong acoustic attenuation, orientation, reflections, or emitter/microphone alignment effects.
- All remote claims succeeded, and there are no buffer overruns.
- The stack-canary crash occurs after the completed 40 cm sequence, so it remains a separate firmware sequence lifecycle issue, not a direct consequence of signal strength.

